The [[locative case]] is also productive when it comes to [[toponymy|placenames]]. An example is {{lang|nug|Nyimarlanpurruni}} referring to the [[Timber Creek, Northern Territory|Timber Creek area]], which consists of the neuter locative prefix {{lang|nug|nyi-}}, the word for ''"river gum"'', the [[plural]] marker {{lang|nug|-purru}}, and an additional marker of the neuter locative, {{lang|nug|-ni}}.<ref name="patrick_mcconvell_2009" />

